chapter.v:
	the two 

	 pillars and the bowl-shaped capitals that were on top of the two pillars; the two networks covering the two bowl-shaped capitals which were on top of the pillars;
 [Deut. 12:5, 11 s 2 Chr. 6:20] [1 Kin. 3:5; 11:9]

	four hundred 

	 pomegranates for the two networks (two rows of pomegranates for each network, to cover the two bowl-shaped capitals that were on the pillars);
 [Deut. 28:23, 24; 1 Kin. 17:1; 2 Chr. 6:26-28]

	he also 

	 made carts and the lavers on the carts;
 [Deut. 28:10; [Is. 43:7] v 2 Chr. 12:6, 7; [James 4:10] w 2 Chr.]

	one Sea 

	 and twelve oxen under it;
 [2 Chr. 6:20,]

	Thus Solomon 

	 had all the furnishings made for the house of God: the altar of gold and the tables on which was the showbread;
 [Lev. 26:14, 33; [Deut. 28:15, 36]]

	with the 

	 flowers and the lamps and the wick-trimmers of gold, of purest gold;
 [2 Kin. 25:9 f 2 Chr. 29:8 g [Deut. 29:24, 25; Jer. 22:8, 9]]
